### Top Navigation
Use the shared shadcn Base Nova `NavigationMenu` between the Margin identity and theme controls. Provide Reports, Suites, Cases, Harnesses, and Models links with an explicit active state. Keep the row compact, square, and keyboard accessible. At narrow widths, place navigation on its own horizontally scrollable header row. Do not add a marketing navigation bar, logo-centered hero, or CTA cluster.

The app header and navigation containers have no padding. On desktop, navigation
items extend from the top of the window to the header's bottom border. Use
shared vertical dividers with no top or bottom item borders and no gaps between
items. Keep text padding inside links; keep the brand and theme controls inset
within their own content. Place keyboard focus outlines inside the links so
the flush container does not clip them.

### Ledger Home

Center the ledger home content in a constrained reading column. Present Entries,
Income, Expenses, and Net movement as borderless, background-free metrics.
Use vertical separators between adjacent metrics, with two columns on narrow
screens and four on wider screens. Preserve the existing summary calculations
and active date-range filtering.

Below the summary, show recent journal entries with the shared shadcn Trace
primitives, not a calendar or a Continue working card. Display at most 20 real
filtered entries, newest date first; preserve source order for matching dates.
State the displayed and total filtered counts. Each entry shows its payee,
date, account, and amount, with keyboard-accessible source file and journal-line
details. Wrap long names and paths within the reading column.

Keep the existing no-source empty state. When the date range contains no
entries, explain that the user can change the date range instead of displaying
sample activity.

The interactive journal timeline study contains 11 sample-data alternatives in
`demos/journal-timelines.html`. Run
`bunx vite --config demos/vite.config.ts --port 4276 --strictPort` from
